    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling potential of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.** **Gunnar Henderson** leads the unit with an 81.88 efficiency score, benefiting from a favorable matchup against K. Montero despite a lingering 33% rain risk. While **Gunnar Henderson** provides our primary power threat, **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.66) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) offer the most compelling combinations of platoon advantages and exploitable pitching. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** draws a prime matchup against Max Scherzer, whose 5.89 xERA makes him a primary target for our offense, while the projected platoon edge against L. P\u00e9rez vaults **Luis Robert Jr.** into the top tier of today\u2019s starters.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Curtis Mead** on the bench. Despite a solid 53.86 score and a favorable park factor, he ultimately fell short due to the defensive and positional requirements of our optimized lineup, leaving him as the first man out. We are also closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Wade Meckler**; their scores are currently contingent on assumed batting order placements. **Nasim Nunez** provides a necessary floor play at 2B, leveraging the weak 5.89 xERA of Scherzer to offset the negative impact of hitting from the bottom of the order. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (60.99), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.48), and **Jacob Wilson** (62.19) offer balanced contributions, ensuring we maintain consistent production across the 5x5 categories as we look to close the gap in stolen bases and counting stats.",
